  "description": "<p>When doing mvn jetty:run from the fcrepo-webapp directory, inspecting the headers for the repository root resource reveals an acl link relation that points to <a href=\"http://localhost:8080/rest//fcr:acl\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://localhost:8080/rest//fcr:acl</a></p>\n\n<p>This seems to be incorrect</p>\n\n<p>Doing a GET on this resource results in a 405 (Method not allowed)</p>\n\n<p>Doing a HEAD against this resource reveals no LDP headers</p>\n\n<p> </p>\n\n<p>The correct ACL link is likely <a href=\"http://localhost:8080/rest//fcr:acl\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://localhost:8080/rest/fcr:acl</a></p>\n\n<p>N.B.  Due to a bug present in \n    <span class=\"jira-issue-macro resolved\" data-jira-key=\"FCREPO-2825\" >\n                <a href=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/browse/FCREPO-2825\" class=\"jira-issue-macro-key issue-link\"  title=\"Section 5.9:  The default, root ACL is not accessible\" >\n            <img class=\"icon\" src=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/universal_avatar/view/type/issuetype/avatar/10303?size=medium\" />\n            FCREPO-2825\n        </a>\n                                                    <span class=\"aui-lozenge aui-lozenge-subtle aui-lozenge-success jira-macro-single-issue-export-pdf\">Closed</span>\n            </span>\n, the \"correct\" ACL link results in a 404.</p>\n\n<p> </p>",
